1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:08,300
The same app runs in development, testing and production. Settings change, but the code stays the same.

2
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:13,450
Keep settings in environment variables, not in the code.

3
00:00:15,150 --> 00:00:21,025
Keep the same code everywhere, and change only the settings between environments.

4
00:00:21,730 --> 00:00:29,305
Log to standard output, keep servers stateless, and store files and data in managed services.

5
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:40,300
Secrets are the keys to the kingdom. Store them in a secrets manager, never in Git, and give each app only the keys it needs.

6
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:45,725
Rotate them, like changing the locks when a staff member leaves.

